<title>POLAND: Minister lists competitive Polish industries.</title>
<headline>Minister lists competitive Polish industries.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economy Minister Wieslaw Kaczmarek on Thursday unveiled a list of Poland's industrial sectors he thought had the best growth potential and best chances to face foreign competition.</p>
<p>He said the sectors included chemical -- notably pharmaceutical products, oil processing and plastics making -- an electronics for industrial use.</p>
<p>&quot;Consumer electronics has little chance in Poland,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>Other competitive sectors are automotive, medical equipment, textile, wood processing, cable and non-ferrous metals, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no reason to be afraid Western competition regarding these sectors,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Kaczmarek declined to name the worst sectors, which should be gradually wound up -- saying that unprofitable sectors using heavy polluting technologies will be first to disappear.</p>
<p>-- Marcin Grajewski +48 22 653 9700</p>
